lities, unfriendly, eats unhealthily. Candidate B: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills, regarded as pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone when communicating. Candidate C: makes correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. Candidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner.\n\nWe need to discuss candidate A, C, D, as they are under-discussed. We can either agree with B but bring up concerns about other candidates, or challenge B's suitability. Perhaps we can argue that Candidate C's decision speed and attention skills are strong, but communication issues are serious. Or we can bring up Candidate D's responsibility and concentration, but moody and loner may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to reference at least one fact from our notes. Also we need to state our current vote. We can either keep B as provisional recommendation, or shift to another candidate. Let's consider: B has strong reliability and stress, but interpersonal issues. A has leadership and anticipation but unfriendly and unhealthy (maybe reliability concerns). C has quick correct decisions, excellent attention, puts concern for others above everything (good crew cooperation), but communication difficulty and egocentric. D has responsibility, concentration, problem solving, but moody and loner.\n\nWhich candidate best fits overall? The criteria include reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability. B strong on reliability, stress, technical, but communication issues. C strong on decision quality, attention, crew cooperation (puts concern for others), but communication difficulty and egocentric. D strong on responsibility, concentration, problem solving, but moody and loner (crew cooperation). A strong on anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership, but unfriendly and unhealthy (reliability, crew cooperation). So each has trade-offs.\n\nWe could argue that Candidate C's concern for others and excellent attention may outweigh communication difficulty, especially if we can train communication. But egocentric and unwilling to further education may be problematic for adaptability. B's pretentiousness and wrong tone may be more severe for crew cooperation. D's moody and loner also problematic.\n\nMaybe we can suggest that Candidate C is a stronger alternative due to decision quality and attention, and that his concern for others suggests good crew cooperation, while his communication difficulty could be mitigated. So we could shift vote to C.\n\nWe need to reference facts: C makes correct decisions quickly, excellent attention skills, puts concern for others above everything (crew cooperation). Also difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education (concerns). Compare to B's pretentiousness and wrong tone.\n\nThus we can argue that C's strengths align more with decision quality and attention, which are critical for long-distance flights, and his concern for others suggests better crew cooperation than B's pretentiousness. So we might change vote to C.\n\nWe need to state vote in metadata JSON.\n\nThus: PUBLIC_MESSAGE: I appreciate B's strengths but I think C may be better overall because of decision quality and crew concern, despite communication issues.\n\nLet's craft."}
